#! ia 1.0

@intent-shape context
  meaning
    says "Need context — pull the source documents, evidence and prerequisites a request rests on. The Orient framing: select the relevant entity and traverse its relations. Also the safe default when no signal dominates."
    answers "Is this request asking what exists, where it is, or what it means?"
  data
    order 0
  routing
    category relation
    primitive Attention
    tie-precedence 4
    kind-focus [definition, contract]
    lane-focus [definitions, contracts]
    predicate-focus [cite, ground, require]

@intent-shape governance
  meaning
    says "Need governance — pull the rules, boundaries, prohibitions and checks that bear on a request. The Act framing: notice the applicable rule, then infer compliance. First in tie precedence because a missed guardrail is the costliest classification error."
    answers "Is this request asking what is permitted, forbidden or enforced?"
  data
    order 1
  routing
    category rule
    primitive Inference
    tie-precedence 0
    kind-focus [governance, policy, check]
    lane-focus [authority, enforcement]
    predicate-focus [govern, constrain, forbid, enforce]
    priming-order [govern, constrain, forbid, enforce, implement]

@intent-shape execution
  meaning
    says "Need execution — pull the bindings, tools, dispatch paths and inputs a request would run through. The Plan framing: choose the invocation surface. The work verbs (implement, fix, author, write) belong to this shape, not to context."
    answers "Is this request asking how something is run, built or invoked?"
  data
    order 2
  routing
    category capability
    primitive Decision
    tie-precedence 3
    kind-focus [binding, template]
    lane-focus [bindings, templates]
    predicate-focus [implement, trigger, route, consume]

@intent-shape sequence
  meaning
    says "Need sequence — pull the ordering, the blockers and the current version. The framing that infers the next step in a process."
    answers "Is this request asking what comes before, after or instead of something?"
  data
    order 3
  routing
    category process
    primitive Inference
    tie-precedence 1
    kind-focus [contract, binding]
    lane-focus [contracts, bindings]
    predicate-focus [run-before, require, supersede]

@intent-shape learning
  meaning
    says "Need learning — pull the derivation, the outputs and the evidence. The Learn framing: store the proof and learn from the outcome."
    answers "Is this request asking what a run taught, produced or derived from?"
  data
    order 4
  routing
    category evidence
    primitive Learning
    tie-precedence 2
    kind-focus [definition]
    lane-focus [definitions]
    predicate-focus [record-lineage-from, produce, cite]

